00:13:42.000 --> 00:14:21.000
windows. And that left room for an interior that was only 11 feet wide. Slice off a few feet for a hallway, a few for a bathroom, a couple for a coat closet, another for some filing cabinets in an umbrella stand. And he would be asking the quintessential modern titan of American industry to work in a dark cell, better suited for a monk, illuminating a manuscript. Sterns asked all the best architects for a solution. They had built medieval bell towers, come man-hatten bank headquarters. They had made midtown hotels that looked like mountain fortresses. But what Sterns wanted was a flagstaff.
窗户。这样留给内部的空间就只有11英尺宽。再扣除几英尺作走廊、几英尺作浴室、两英尺作衣帽间，还要留出空间放文件柜和雨伞架。而他却在要求现代美国工业的典型巨头们在一个更适合僧侣手抄经文的黑暗牢房里工作。斯特恩斯向所有最优秀的建筑师寻求解决方案。他们建造过中世纪的钟楼，设计过曼哈顿的银行总部。他们建造过看起来像山地城堡的中城区酒店。但斯特恩斯想要的却是一根旗杆。

