of out? He told Sterns that if he did this, the walls wouldn't have to be 5 feet thick. They could be 9 inches. And in the 20-foot wide office spaces that that would create, the quintessential modern Titan of American industry would have room to stretch out his legs, while he made out his rent-check to John Noble Sterns. They would call it the tower building. Sterns loved the idea.
